  "worked_solution": "First, we plot the graph of $y={8}^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220062/assets/d1d90ab26cf9c3939b355a781b2192f962204b077b990b6a142db642a1316f4f.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y={8}^{x}+0.5,$ we take the graph of $y={8}^{x}$ and shift it $0.5$ units up. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,1.5),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=0.5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220062/assets/452f0482708656146b2e5cd7f58832250fc95e25707cacb66800255aee977b21.png)",
